%S A397949 2,3,12,10,9,8,6,5,18,17,44,43,324,606,604,765,762,759,756,757,1380,
%T A397949 1381,1435,1630,1628,1626,2318,2316,2314,2310,2308,2306,2304,2301,
%U A397949 2298,2295,2292,2289,2286,2284,2280,2277,2274,2272,12110,12108,12105,12102,12099
%N A397949 The least number k such that the n-th iterate of k under x -> x + omega(x) is the first prime encountered in its trajectory.
%e A397949 a(1) = 2, because the first iterate of 2, namely 3 is prime.
%e A397949 a(2) = 3, because the first iterate of 3, namely 4, is composite, but the 2nd iterate 5 is prime.
%e A397949 a(8) = 5, because the first 7 iterates of 5, [6, 8, 9, 10, 12, 14, 16] are composite, but the 8th iterate 17 is prime.
%e A397949 No lesser numbers have this property.
%Y A397949 Cf. A000040, A001221, A229109.
%K A397949 nonn
%O A397949 1,1
%A A397949 _Jean-Marc Rebert_, Jul 16 2026
